                  <msItem>
                     <title>Annales ad annum 1268</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">The inscription at foot of the last leaf is
                        carefully written in the same hand as the inscription in Digby 37. The
                        others are probably scribbles of later date.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Fol. iii recto has 'Contenta huius libri
                        Exposicio Britonis in libros universalium porphyrii', but this is not now in
                        the MS. </note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">For the annals see cards under Ramsey and
                        Huntingdon, and for E. de T. fellow of Oriel c. 1350--1360, cf. Auct.
                        F.v.28, Digby 37 (Oriel 4).</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Also on fol. iii recto is the scribble
                        'Baccalarii huius dominus ha[...] dominus owde dominus northe [...] in
                        probatione dominus edwardes dominus rod[...] anno domini 1o 5o 0o 7o [but
                        this must be 1547: see Richards and Shadwell, p. 64]'.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Oxford binding c. 1600.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
